        "findings": "VERDICT: LGTM\n\nThe change slots cleanly into an established pattern and adds nothing out of place:\n\n- `Owner.membershipTier(Integer, String)` is a static derivation method sitting right alongside its siblings `householdId(...)` and `membershipNumber(...)`, with matching Javadoc style (\"deterministic in those two fields\"). The derivation logic lives in the domain model, which is where the existing derived fields put it.\n- `OwnerMapper.formatMembershipTier(owner)` mirrors `formatMembershipNumber`/`formatHouseholdId` exactly \u2014 same null-guard, same delegation to the `Owner` static method, same `@Mapping(... expression ...)` wiring. No logic is duplicated; the mapper stays a thin adapter and the model owns the rule.\n- The `openapi.yml` entry is added next to `membershipNumber` with the same `readOnly`/`title`/`description`/`example` shape used by the neighboring derived fields.\n\nLogic is in the right unit, nothing is duplicated, and neither `Owner` nor `OwnerMapper` is turning into a catch-all \u2014 each just gains one more member of an existing family. A maintainer of this codebase would find it natural."
